Notebook[{
Cell["The Golden Quadruple — R3 Computational Companion","Title"],
Cell["Michał Przybylski","Subtitle"],
Cell["R3 docs-only review draft; not newly executed. User-provided Codex report (2026-11-07 Europe/Warsaw): R2 kernel tests 12/12 fresh and contaminated, not full graphical notebook validation. No output cells are supplied. Review all cells in a working graphical front end, fresh and with u=2;t=0 set beforehand.","Text"],
Cell["Sources: https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.00973v2 ; https://zenodo.org/records/23919863 . Configuration and difference multiset are classical. New executable code only is MIT, copyright 2026 Michał Przybylski, author decision 2026-11-07 Europe/Warsaw; see LICENSE. Prose and third-party material are excluded; paper retains its own CC BY 4.0.","Text"],
Cell["Maintenance correction 2026-11-07 (Europe/Warsaw): final semicolons removed from sections 1–3 to display results instead of Null. User reports GUI success. Supplied CZYTAJ.txt reports 12/12 kernel tests fresh and with u=2;t=0, not independently reproduced here. Full GUI evaluation in both conditions remains unconfirmed. ToExpression and NotebookDirectory[] dependency unchanged.","Text"],
Cell["1. Exact example — u=1, F=phi^4","Section"],
Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"ToExpression","[","\"(* Author: Michał Przybylski. AI-assisted R2 draft: this revision UNEXECUTED in Wolfram Language.\\n Sources: https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.00973v2 ; https://zenodo.org/records/23919863\\n Classical configuration, not claimed as a new discovery. *)\\nClearAll[phi, positiveDifferences, rhoMinus, rhoPlus, cSum, cClosed,\\n u0,f0,points,differences,expected,multiplicities,residualTable,pairCheck,\\n identityCheck,illustration,numericalError,symbolicChecks,fibonacciShiftCheck,\\n root,report,s,z,v,x,n,uu,tt,k];\\n(* u and t deliberately remain untouched: all symbolic checks localize their variables. *)\\nphi=(1+Sqrt[5])/2;\\n(* Real u>0, F>(phi+phi^2)u. Concrete example u=1, F=phi^4. *)\\nu0=1; f0=phi^4;\\npoints=FullSimplify[{f0,f0-phi,f0-phi^2,f0-phi-phi^2}];\\n(* One entry per unordered pair: do not remove duplicates. *)\\npositiveDifferences[s_List]:=FullSimplify[Abs[Subtract@@#]]& /@ Subsets[s,{2}];\\ndifferences=Sort[positiveDifferences[points], TrueQ[FullSimplify[#1 < #2]] &];\\nexpected={1,phi,phi,phi^2,phi^2,phi^3};\\nmultiplicities=Table[Count[differences,z_ /; TrueQ[FullSimplify[z-v] == 0]],{v,{1,phi,phi^2,phi^3}}];\\n{points,differences,multiplicities}\\n\"","]"}]],"Input"],
Cell["2. Fibonacci residuals — integer n>=2","Section"],
Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"ToExpression","[","\"(* Real x>1, u>0; integer n>=2, Fib[0]=0, Fib[1]=1. *)\\nrhoMinus[x_,u_]:=(x^2-x-1)u;\\nrhoPlus[x_,u_]:=x (x^2-x-1)u;\\nresidualTable=Table[With[{x=Fibonacci[n+1]/Fibonacci[n]},\\n {n,x,rhoMinus[x,1],rhoPlus[x,1]}],{n,2,12}];\\n(* Exact claimed values: (-1)^n u/Fibonacci[n]^2 and\\n (-1)^n Fibonacci[n+1]u/Fibonacci[n]^3. Finite checks are not proofs. *)\\nresidualTable\\n\"","]"}]],"Input"],
Cell["3. Six-pair cosine sum and illustration","Section"],
Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"ToExpression","[","\"(* Real t; real u>0. Each of the SIX positive pair differences contributes. *)\\ncSum[uu_,tt_]:=Cos[2 Pi uu tt]+2 Cos[2 Pi phi uu tt]+\\n 2 Cos[2 Pi phi^2 uu tt]+Cos[2 Pi phi^3 uu tt];\\ncClosed[uu_,tt_]:=8 Cos[Pi phi uu tt]^2 Cos[Pi phi^2 uu tt]^2-2;\\nsymbolicChecks[]:=Module[{uu,tt}, {\\n FullSimplify[Total[Cos[2 Pi # tt]& /@ differences]-cSum[1,tt],\\n   Assumptions->Element[tt,Reals]],\\n FullSimplify[TrigExpand[cSum[uu,tt]-cClosed[uu,tt]],\\n   Assumptions->Element[{uu,tt},Reals]&&uu>0]}];\\n{pairCheck,identityCheck}=symbolicChecks[];\\n(* tau_8=Fib[8]/u; for u=1, tau_8=21 and 21 phi=34-phi^-8.\\n   This follows from Fib[n+1]-phi Fib[n]=(-phi^-1)^n. *)\\nfibonacciShiftCheck=FullSimplify[21 phi-(34-phi^-8)];\\n(* Finite illustration only: not a proof of almost periodicity or a supremum. *)\\nillustration=Module[{tt}, Plot[Evaluate[{cSum[1,tt],cSum[1,tt+Fibonacci[8]]}],{tt,-10,10},\\n WorkingPrecision->40,PlotPoints->120,MaxRecursion->4,PlotRange->{-2,6},\\n PlotLegends->{\\\"C_S(t)\\\",\\\"C_S(t+21)\\\"},AxesLabel->{\\\"t\\\",\\\"C_S\\\"}]];\\n(* Evaluate arguments numerically first: independent floating-point evaluation. *)\\nnumericalError=Max[Table[With[{tt=N[k/20,50]},\\n Abs[cSum[1,tt]-cClosed[1,tt]]],{k,-200,200}]];\\n{pairCheck,identityCheck,numericalError}\\n\"","]"}]],"Input"],
Cell["For u=1, tau8=Fibonacci[8]=21 and 21 phi=34-phi^-8. The finite plot is illustrative, not a proof of almost periodicity or a global supremum.","Text"],
Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"ToExpression","[","\"illustration\"","]"}]],"Input"],
Cell["Validation. Save next to the WL file and Tests/. The runner recomputes definitions, prints TestReport, and exports a local PNG. Inspect all messages. Tests do not substitute for proofs.","Text"],
Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"ToExpression","[","\"Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[],\\\"GoldenQuadruple.wl\\\"}]]\"","]"}]],"Input"],
Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"ToExpression","[","\"Block[{u=2,t=0},symbolicChecks[]]\"","]"}]],"Input"]
},WindowTitle->"Golden Quadruple R3 — review",StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb"]
